Say what keeps the matching loop going

doServiceMatch() loops while keepGuessing is true, and keepGuessing is true
when either a nested startMatching put the nub back into the need-config
state (r) or the catalogue changed under us (g), which means a kext was
loaded or unloaded while we were matching.

The panel shows the same few services matching over and over, so this prints
the nub and the two reasons, but only on the iterations that really repeat:
the nubs that match once stay quiet.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index bfc0ad8..9b29006 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -5410,6 +5410,13 @@ IOService::doServiceMatch( IOOptionBits options )
 		    && (0 == (__state[0] & kIOServiceInactiveState));
 
 		if (keepGuessing) {
+			/* nio: this loop is the one that repeats.  Say which nub
+			 * repeats and why: r = a nested startMatching put the nub
+			 * back into the need-config state, g = the catalogue
+			 * changed, i.e. a kext loaded or unloaded under us. */
+			printf("\nnio: D %s r=%d g=%d", getName() ? getName() : "?",
+			    (int)reRegistered,
+			    (int)(catalogGeneration != gIOCatalogue->getGenerationCount()));
 			unlockForArbitration();
 		}
 	}
